A view reads another view, and only the inner one changes: it alone is
made again, and the outer one reads it as before.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE VIEW cheap AS SELECT id, name FROM dish WHERE price_kr < 100;
CREATE VIEW cheap_names AS SELECT name FROM cheap;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup', 95);

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE VIEW cheap AS SELECT id, name FROM dish WHERE price_kr < 80;
CREATE VIEW cheap_names AS SELECT name FROM cheap;

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, 2 steps
  view `cheap`: changed in schema.sql
    DROP VIEW "cheap"
  view `cheap`: as schema.sql makes it
    CREATE VIEW cheap AS SELECT id, name FROM dish WHERE price_kr < 80
